{"market": "6J", "market_name": "Japanese yen", "strategy_key": "squeeze_breakout_v4", "strategy_name": "BB/KC squeeze · v4", "variant": null, "variant_label": null, "stability_mode": "local_perturbation", "validation_rules": {"min_net_return": 0.0, "min_sharpe": 0.3, "max_drawdown": -0.3, "min_completed_trades": 40}, "run_id": "cb_bbkc_6j_v4_15m", "generated_at": "2026-11-11T19:52:50+00:00", "periods": {"dev": ["2018-01-01", "2022-12-31"], "val": ["2023-01-01", "2024-12-31"]}, "strategy": {"summary": "Trade the breakout after the market goes quiet, flat by the close. Bollinger Bands (2 standard deviations of the last L closes) sitting inside a Keltner Channel (the same average ± a multiple of ATR) mark a squeeze: price is moving less than its usual range. The first close (or touch) outside that quiet range decides the direction: above goes long, below goes short. A stop at the other side of the box or a fixed ATR distance, an optional profit target, and everything closed at the session's last close.", "formula": "squeeze when 2 × stdev(close, L) < Keltner width × ATR(L); box = high / low of the squeeze bars", "rules": [{"label": "Enter", "text": "A bar is a squeeze bar when the Bollinger Bands over the last L bars fit inside the Keltner Channel. A run of squeeze bars (at least the minimum, never across the open) makes a box: its highest high and lowest low. The box stays live for 1 or 4 bars after the last compression bar (any box width). Close entry: a bar closes outside the box, filled at the next bar's open. Wick entry: a stop order rests at the box edge and fills the moment price trades through it, at the worse of the bar's open and the edge. The first breakout uses up the box, even when a filter blocks the trade (wrong direction, against the EMA(50) trend, a position already open, or the last 30 minutes of the session)."}, {"label": "Exit", "text": "Stop at the far side of the box, or 1.5 × ATR(14) from the entry. Optional target at 1 or 2.5 times that risk. Both are live inside each bar; a bar touching both counts as the stop. Anything still open is closed at the session's last close."}, {"label": "Size", "text": "Long only or both ways; one position at a time, never held overnight. As many whole 6J contracts as the account covers at full contract value (no leverage), starting from $1,000,000."}], "axes": [{"label": "Bar size", "values": ["15min"]}, {"label": "Squeeze length (bars)", "values": ["15", "25", "35", "45"]}, {"label": "Keltner width (× ATR)", "values": ["1.5", "2", "2.5", "3", "3.5"]}, {"label": "Min squeeze bars", "values": ["1", "4"]}, {"label": "Entry", "values": ["close", "wick"]}, {"label": "Setup live for (bars)", "values": ["1", "4"]}, {"label": "Stop", "values": ["box", "1.5 ATR"]}, {"label": "Target (× risk)", "values": ["1R", "2.5R", "none"]}, {"label": "Direction", "values": ["long", "both"]}, {"label": "Trend filter", "values": ["none", "EMA 50"]}, {"label": "Min box width (× ATR)", "values": ["any"]}], "grid_size": 3840, "length_note": "All lengths are in bars of the chosen bar size; the minimum box width is in ATR(14)."}, "funnel": [{"name": "Start", "sub": "every combination", "n": 3840, "why": "All 3,840 versions backtested once on 2018–2022 data."}, {"name": "1 · Integrity", "sub": "no cheating", "n": 3840, "why": "Per-trade checks on every version: the box came only from earlier bars, the breakout was the squeeze's first, fills were never better than the market, nothing was held overnight. Plus 40 random versions re-run on cut-off data. 0 failed."}, {"name": "2 · Enough trades", "sub": "≥100 trades, spread out", "n": 3258, "why": "Needs ≥100 completed trades and ≥10 a year in ≥4 of the 5 years. Removed 582 (582 on 15min)."}, {"name": "3 · Profit", "sub": "net > 0, Sharpe ≥ 0.75", "n": 4, "why": "Needs a net profit, Sharpe ≥ 0.75 and drawdown no worse than 30%. Removed 3,254 (3,254 on 15min); 2,702 of them lost money."}, {"name": "4 · Stable settings", "sub": "nudged settings also work", "n"